    "title": "‘Daredevil’s Vincent D’Onofrio Explains Why Kingpin Won’t Appear In ‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’",
    "text": "Vincent D'Onofrio (R) explained why his Kingpin won't appear in 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' Matt Kennedy/Sony Pictures Releasing/Marvel Entertainment/David Giesbrecht/Netflix/Courtesy Everett Collection As the MCU prepares to revisit a few familiar faces, don’t expect Vincent D’Onofrio’s Wilson ‘Kingpin’ Fisk to make an appearance. The Daredevil: Born Again actor recently explained why his villainous character won’t make an appearance in Spider-Man: Brand New Day, despite rumors that Fisk is now mayor of NYC in the MCU. “No. I think I’ll just wait until they have the rights to my character and they put me in one of those movies, and then I’ll figure it all out,” said D’Onofrio on The Playlist’s Bingeworthy podcast. Whereas the upcoming Spider-Man installment is the latest from Marvel Studios, Season 2 of Daredevil: Born Again comes from Marvel Television, set for a March 24 premiere on Disney+. D’Onofrio returns as Fisk in the series after first playing the role on the Netflix parent series Daredevil from 2015 to 2018. Watch on Deadline Visit Advertiser websiteGO TO PAGE In December, Spider-Man: Brand New Day director Destin Daniel Cretton revealed that the much anticipated fourth installment in the MCU’s Spider-Man franchise has completed filming on the upcoming prelude to Avengers: Doomsday, set to premiere July 31 in theaters. Charlie Cox and Vincent D’Onofrio in ‘Daredevil’ Netflix/Courtesy Everett Collection Helmed by Cretton (Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings), producers include Amy Pascal and Marvel Studios head Kevin Feige returning. Zendaya will reprise her role as MJ, with Sadie Sink and Liza Colón-Zayas also joining the cast in undisclosed roles. Must Read Stories Read More About: Subscribe to Deadline Get our Breaking News Alerts and Keep your inbox happy. Sign Up",
